# Data conversion between kilobyte and tebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between kilobyte and tebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1KB to 0.0000TiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KB yields 0.0000TiB; backward, converting 1TiB to 1099511627.776KB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5TiB yields 1649267441.664KB. Tiny magnitudes round to four fractional digits.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1KB
print(forward_whole->to(TiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KB
print(forward_fractional->to(TiB))
backward_whole: int = 1TiB
print(backward_whole->to(KB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5TiB
print(backward_fractional->to(KB))

<<< stdout
0.0000TiB
0.0000TiB
1099511627.776KB
1649267441.664KB

<<< stderr
